**How to implement.** The experiment matrix at the top of the Data step, a data badge per experiment in each cell (001 §O 'Experiment matrix view: rows source × objects × φ, columns analyzer, with a data badge per cell'; the S9.3 brief; S9.1's badges). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S9.3. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs`, each with a one-line doc: `type MatrixRowKey with member this.caption : ControlCaption`, its sources' labels joined by ` + ` (or `—`), ` · `, then its objects as `<label>@<angle.degreeCaption>` (step 280) joined by ` → ` (or `—`); `type MatrixColumnKey with member this.caption : ControlCaption`, its analyzers' labels joined by ` + ` (or `—`); and on `ConstructorUiId` `static member experimentMatrixEntry (experimentId : ExperimentId) : ConstructorUiId` (`ExperimentMatrixEntry_<id>`). (2) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`, in the Data step group: `experimentMatrix` (`"ExperimentMatrix"`), with a one-line doc. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/DataStepView.fs`: first in the panel, the heading `Experiment matrix:` and a `Grid` carrying `experimentMatrix` over `ExperimentMatrix.ofExperiments model.experimentCollection.experiments model.kitSetups model.kitItems` (step 322): its first row the columns' captions, then one row per matrix row, its caption first and then, per column, a vertical `StackPanel` holding, for each experiment of that cell, a verb carrying `experimentMatrixEntry id` that reads `<name> · <model.dataBadgeOf experiment's text>` and sends `ReviewExperimentData id` (step 315), the reviewed experiment's on the positive background; an empty cell holds nothing. When `unplaced` is not empty, a wrapping line `Not in the matrix (setup missing): <their names joined by ", ">`. With no experiment, the line `(no experiments yet)`. No other control or message is added. Tests, in `DataStepTests`: `the Data step UiIds are the stable intent-named ids` also pins `ExperimentMatrix` and `ExperimentMatrixEntry_1`. New `the matrix shows each experiment in its row and column with its data badge, and lists the unplaced ones`: over the class's model holding E1 over `Setup 1`, E2 over `Bench B` (its polarizer turned) and E3 over `Gone` revision 1, the grid holds the row captions of `Setup 1` and `Bench B`, E1's entry reading `E1 · no data` and E2's `E2 · no data`, and the line naming `E3`; after E1's data is attached through the class's mock, E1's entry reads `E1 · validated (3 points)`. With trait `ui-smoke`, `pressing a matrix entry reviews that experiment`: pressing E2's entry in the rendered Data step reviews E2 and shows `dataReviewPanel`. `ScrollExtentTests`: `the kit window's Data step leaves everything reachable` (step 323) also holds a pending split of three groups, a reviewed experiment of three points, one excluded, with one correction, and the matrix of three experiments, its assertion kept.

**Acceptance.** After the matrix view lands, the Data step MUST open on the experiment matrix, each experiment in the row of its sources and objects with their angles and the column of its analyzers, showing its data badge and reviewing it when pressed, the experiments whose setup the kit lacks listed apart; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `pressing a matrix entry reviews that experiment`, the count rising by 1; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `the matrix shows each experiment in its row and column with its data badge, and lists the unplaced ones`, the count rising by 1, and the changed `the Data step UiIds are the stable intent-named ids` and `the kit window's Data step leaves everything reachable`; and build, elevation and the sixteen s31 invariants MUST pass.
